## About us

This website, juniperhealth.app, is run by Neil Hyde, a sole trader trading as **Juniper Health** ("we", "us" and "our").

{% businessDetails /%}

## Our information is general, not advice

Our guides and self-checks give **general information** about health conditions and UK disability benefits. They are written in plain English to help you understand your options.

- They are **not medical advice.** Always talk to your GP or another qualified health professional about your own health. In an emergency, call 999.
- They are **not legal or financial advice.** For advice about your own situation, contact Citizens Advice, a welfare rights service or another qualified adviser.
- We are **not part of the Department for Work and Pensions (DWP)**, the NHS, Social Security Scotland or any other government body.

## Our self-checks give estimates only

Our PIP, Attendance Allowance and DLA self-checks give an **estimate** based on your answers and on the rules as we understand them.

- Only the **DWP** (or the relevant government body) can decide whether you get a benefit, and how much.
- The result depends on the answers you give. The DWP will make its own decision based on your claim form, evidence and any assessment.
- A result saying you may qualify does **not** mean you will. A result saying you may not qualify does **not** mean you should not claim.

## Keeping our information accurate

We work hard to keep our information correct and up to date, and we check each page at least once a year. Benefit rules and rates change, and mistakes can happen. We cannot promise that everything is always complete, correct or current. Please check important facts with official sources, such as GOV.UK and the NHS.

If you spot something wrong, please [tell us](/contact/).

## Links to other websites

We link to other websites, such as GOV.UK, the NHS and charities, because we think they are helpful. We are not responsible for the content of websites we do not run.

Some links are **affiliate links**. We always label these clearly. See [how we make money](/affiliate-disclosure/).

## Using our content

The words, design and tools on this website belong to us, unless we say otherwise. You are welcome to:

- read, print and save pages for your own use
- share links to our pages
- quote short parts of our guides, as long as you credit Juniper Health and link to the page

Please do not copy whole pages or our tools onto another website, or use our content for commercial purposes, without asking us first.

## Things you must not do

You must not:

- use the website for anything unlawful
- try to break, overload or gain unauthorised access to the website
- copy our self-checks or use automated tools to scrape the site

## Our responsibility to you

We provide this website free of charge. We are not responsible for any loss that happens because you relied on information on this website, as long as we acted with reasonable care.

Nothing in these terms limits our responsibility where it would be unlawful to do so, including for death or personal injury caused by our negligence, or for fraud. Nothing in these terms affects your legal rights as a consumer.

## If the website is unavailable

We aim to keep the website running at all times, but we cannot promise it will always be available or free from errors.

